p.src:
The key to contraction is the chain rule. Because the coordinate maps are inverse, $\frac{\partial x^b}{\partial y^m}
 \frac{\partial y^m}{\partial x^a}
 =
 \frac{\partial x^b}{\partial x^a}
 =\delta^b{}_a.$ The two Jacobian matrices are inverses, and their product is the Kronecker delta.

