p.src:
A quick proof makes the notation transparent. For any scalar function $f$, $\frac{\partial f}{\partial y^m}
 \frac{\partial y^m}{\partial x^a}
 =\frac{\partial f}{\partial x^a}.$ Choosing $f=x^b$ gives $\frac{\partial x^b}{\partial y^m}
 \frac{\partial y^m}{\partial x^a}
 =\frac{\partial x^b}{\partial x^a}
 =\delta^b{}_a.$

