p.src:
In two dimensions this means $\begin{pmatrix}
 g_{11} & g_{12}\\
 g_{12} & g_{22}
 \end{pmatrix}
 \begin{pmatrix}
 g^{11} & g^{12}\\
 g^{12} & g^{22}
 \end{pmatrix}
 =
 \begin{pmatrix}
 1&0\\
 0&1
 \end{pmatrix}.$ For example, $\begin{aligned}
 g_{11}g^{11}+g_{12}g^{12}&=1,\\
 g_{11}g^{12}+g_{12}g^{22}&=0.\end{aligned}$ The other row supplies the remaining two equations.

